-- ~/.config/cachix/cachix.dhall — the Cachix CLI's own config file.
--
-- `authToken` is resolved from Bitwarden Secrets Manager (BWS) at `chezmoi
-- apply` time. It previously held the literal string "CACHIX_AUTH_TOKEN" — a
-- placeholder, not a token — which silently broke every consumer that reads
-- this file, including devenv's documented keyring -> cachix.dhall fallback.
--
-- Which token to use here: the BWS item is cache-scoped (`"scopes": "cache"`)
-- and authenticates against the caches we actually pull from (cattivi-public,
-- devenv, pi, nix-community all return 200). Do not substitute the token that
-- lives in the macOS keychain under
-- secretspec/devenv-cachix/default/CACHIX_AUTH_TOKEN: that one is `"scopes":
-- "tx"` and 401s on the same endpoints, so it grants nothing. If a token here
-- ever starts 401ing, check the scope claim in its JWT payload before assuming
-- the file is wrong.
--
-- This item ID is BWS key `CACHIX_AUTH_TOKEN`. The value is read through
-- chezmoi's `bitwardenSecrets` template function, the same mechanism the
-- Raycast and Hermes templates use, so nothing in git holds the secret.
--
-- Dhall needs the quotes: authToken is a Text field.
{ authToken = "{{ (bitwardenSecrets "7d5939fa-cb7f-4c77-bfe8-b4b4010442e8").value }}"
, hostname = "https://cachix.org"
-- binaryCaches holds per-cache signing keys for *pushing* to a cache. Empty
-- means we push with no key of our own; pulls authenticate via authToken above
-- plus the public keys already declared in modules/infra/nix/caches.nix.
, binaryCaches = [] : List { name : Text, secretKey : Text }
}
